## Synchronous Functions
Synchronous code executes line by line.

Each statement waits until previous statement finishes.

Example
console.log("Task 1");
console.log("Task 2");
console.log("Task 3");

Output
Task 1
Task 2
Task 3

## Asynchronous Functions

Asynchronous code does not block execution.

Tasks can run in background.

Examples:

API calls
Timers
File loading
Example Using setTimeout()
File Name: asynchronousExample.js
console.log("Start");

setTimeout(() => {

    console.log("Inside Timeout");

}, 2000);

console.log("End");

Output
Start
End
Inside Timeout